{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The transfer-overlap run remained joint through 30 ticks and exited after a new entry applied. That supports the missing-retry hypothesis, but does not establish a justified liveness bound.\n\nIt also exposed a separate discrepancy: `ApplyConfChange` reported `AutoLeave=true`, while `Status.Config` reported false. `Config.Clone`, which Status uses, omits that field. I’ll check this narrower copy-preservation duty with a fresh fixed artifact.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > status_autoleave_test.go <<'EOF'\npackage raft\nimport (\n \\\"encoding/json\\\"\n \\\"fmt\\\"\n \\\"testing\\\"\n pb \\\"go.etcd.io/raft/v3/raftpb\\\"\n)\nfunc TestAssuranceStatusAutoLeaveCopy(t *testing.T) {\n for _,implicit:=range []bool{true,false} {\n  name:=\\\"explicit\\\"; transition:=pb.ConfChangeTransitionJointExplicit\n  if implicit {name=\\\"implicit\\\";transition=pb.ConfChangeTransitionJointImplicit}\n  t.Run(name,func(t *testing.T) {\n   emit:=func(v map[string]interface{}) {v[\\\"case\\\"]=name;v[\\\"node\\\"]=uint64(1);b,err:=json.Marshal(v);if err\"'!=nil {t.Fatal(err)};fmt.Println(\"CA_EVENT \"+string(b))}\n   st:=NewMemoryStorage()\n   if err:=st.ApplySnapshot(pb.Snapshot{Metadata:pb.SnapshotMetadata{Index:1,Term:1,ConfState:pb.ConfState{Voters:[]uint64{1}}}});err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n   if err:=st.SetHardState(pb.HardState{Term:1,Commit:1});err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n   rn,err:=NewRawNode(&Config{ID:1,Storage:st,Applied:1,ElectionTick:10,HeartbeatTick:1,MaxSizePerMsg:4096,MaxInflightMsgs:256})\n   if err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n   applied:=uint64(1);observed:=false\n   pump:=func() {\n    for step:=0;step<100 && rn.HasReady();step++ {\n     rd:=rn.Ready()\n     if !IsEmptySnap(rd.Snapshot) {t.Fatal(\"unexpected snapshot\")}\n     if err:=st.Append(rd.Entries);err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n     if !IsEmptyHardState(rd.HardState) {if err:=st.SetHardState(rd.HardState);err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}}\n     for _,e:=range rd.CommittedEntries {\n      if e.Index!=applied+1 {t.Fatal(\"apply order\")}\n      if e.Type==pb.EntryConfChangeV2 {\n       var cc pb.ConfChangeV2;if err:=cc.Unmarshal(e.Data);err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n       cs:=rn.ApplyConfChange(cc)\n       // Observe only the entering operation, by its nonempty Changes identity;\n       // this selects both true and false modes independently of the result.\n       if len(cc.Changes)>0 {\n        if observed {t.Fatal(\"duplicate entering change\")};observed=true\n        emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"configuration_installed\",\"index\":e.Index,\"auto_leave\":cs.AutoLeave,\"outgoing_count\":len(cs.VotersOutgoing)})\n        status:=rn.Status()\n        emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"status_copy\",\"index\":e.Index,\"auto_leave\":status.Config.AutoLeave,\"outgoing_count\":len(status.Config.Voters[1]),\"observed\":true})\n       }\n      } else if e.Type!=pb.EntryNormal {t.Fatal(\"unexpected entry\")}\n      applied=e.Index\n     }\n     // Outgoing messages can target the newly added learner 2. They are\n     // dropped by the isolated transport; all voters are node 1 in both sets.\n     rn.Advance(rd)\n    }\n    if rn.HasReady() {t.Fatal(\"work bound exceeded\")}\n   }\n   if err:=rn.Campaign();err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)};pump()\n   if rn.Status().RaftState!=StateLeader {t.Fatal(\"election failed\")}\n   cc:=pb.ConfChangeV2{Transition:transition,Changes:[]pb.ConfChangeSingle{{Type:pb.ConfChangeAddLearnerNode,NodeID:2}}}\n   if err:=rn.ProposeConfChange(cc);err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)};pump()\n   if !observed {t.Fatal(\"configuration was not applied\")}\n   emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"run_completed\",\"applied\":applied})\n  })\n }\n}\nEOF\ncat > build_status_check.py <<'\"'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']));m['version']=r['audit_spec_version']\nssnew=[dict(id='s-config-clone',file='tracker/tracker.go',start_line=95,end_line=113,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s-auto-field-contract',file='tracker/tracker.go',start_line=26,end_line=34,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='s-status-config-copy',file='status.go',start_line=25,end_line=76,kind='code_observation')]\nfor bid in ['b-membership','b-reconstruction']:\n b=next(x for x in m['behaviors'] if x['id']==bid);b.setdefault('produces_fact_ids',[]).append('f-auto-leave-policy')\nm['behaviors'].append(dict(id='b-status-copy',primary_activity='A7',execution_owner='RawNode.Status -> getStatus -> tracker.Config.Clone',protocol_context='Installed tracker configuration at synchronous observation',trigger='Status request',source_ids=['s-status-config-copy','s-config-clone','s-auto-field-contract'],consumes_fact_ids=['f-auto-leave-policy'],reads=['Current tracker.Config'],external_effects=['Returns copied voter and learner maps in Status.Config'],important_branches=['Config.Clone initializes copied map fields but does not assign AutoLeave, so the copy receives false regardless of the original true policy.'],cross_activity_effects={'A4':'Reports the policy distinguishing automatic from application-controlled joint exit.'},unknowns=[]))\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='f-auto-leave-policy',meaning='Installed tracker.Config.AutoLeave records whether Raft should automatically leave the current joint configuration; it is distinct from whether joint exit has already happened.',identity={'node':'Raft instance','configuration':'Installed joint configuration'},validity_context='EnterJoint sets the requested policy; LeaveJoint clears it. Status observation does not change the installed configuration.',representation=['tracker.Config.AutoLeave','ApplyConfChange returned ConfState.AutoLeave'],durability='Caller records configuration including policy in snapshots; status is a volatile observation.',recovery='ConfState restoration feeds AutoLeave to EnterJoint.',source_ids=['s-config-changer','s-config-restore','s-auto-field-contract','s-config'],unknowns=[]))\na=next(x for x in m['activities'] if x['class_id']=='A7');a['behavior_ids'].append('b-status-copy');a['source_ids']+=['s-status-config-copy','s-config-clone'];a['realization_summary']+='; Status returns a copied configuration including its automatic-exit policy.'\nb=next(x for x in m['behaviors'] if x['id']=='b-application');b['unknowns']=[x for x in b['unknowns'] if not x.startswith('Whether a failed transfer')];b['important_branches'].append('After automatic-exit proposal rejection during transfer, timeout clears the transfer field but does not call appliedTo. Further application is an independent retry trigger; heartbeat-only processing does not directly retry.')\nm['surfaces'].append(dict(entry_point='tracker.Config.Clone -> Status.Config.AutoLeave',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b-status-copy'],reason='Determine whether status preserves installed automatic-exit policy; clone copies maps but omits the scalar AutoLeave field.',source_ids=['s-config-clone','s-status-config-copy','s-auto-field-contract'],high_consequence=False))\njson.dump(m,open('status-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='Does Status preserve the installed AutoLeave policy when copying a joint configuration, including both implicit and explicit transition modes?',importance='Incorrect status can misreport who is responsible for completing a joint transition. This is a configuration-observation defect; effects on decisions by external operators are not established.',trigger_rationale='The auto-exit exploration reported true from ApplyConfChange and false from Status for the same joint configuration. Source identifies Config.Clone omission, so a fresh direct comparison between established ConfState and immediate Status can isolate copy preservation without inventing a liveness bound.',source_ids=[],participants=['Raft instance','Status caller'],objects=['Installed AutoLeave','Returned Status.Config'],contexts=['Applied implicit or explicit joint configuration','No intervening transition between installation and observation'],event_paths=['ProposeConfChange -> committed entry -> ApplyConfChange -> immediate Status -> Config.Clone'],activity_classes=['A4','A7'],behavior_ids=['b-membership','b-reconstruction','b-status-copy'],fact_ids=['f-auto-leave-policy'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b-context':'Actual election supplies the authority to commit configuration.','b-ready':'Ordered Ready persistence and application establish legal installation.'},obligation_r